wer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389515} {:answer/id #uuid "8d89ca9e-8cf1-5b9c-a38d-3f29dfc620a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389516} {:answer/id #uuid "7881fdc3-f1e6-5655-83ea-d156cd6e11c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d89ca9e-8cf1-5b9c-a38d-3f29dfc620a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389516} :answer-field/id #uuid "b92fac85-7a9a-5915-90d4-a283e5eef049" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "38414465-84de-53ed-9f2d-540277ea9f01" :question/math-academy-id "q-164439" :question/problem "$$\nf(t,z)=⟨3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\text{_____},\\,z⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(t,z)$ above parametrizes one sheet of the hyperbolic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $2{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}=18$ for $x\\ge 3.$ What is the second component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the hyperbola\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}=18\\,⇒\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nfor $x\\ge 3$ in $xy$-plane has the parametrization\n\n$$\n⟨x,y⟩=⟨3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})\n$$\n\nsince \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & =\\frac{(3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9{sec}^{2}⁡t}{9}-\\frac{2{tan}^{2}⁡t}{2} \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡t-{tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t,z) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and $z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the second component of $f$ is $\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389518 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "043304f9-3a42-53ad-8538-3cea955fe040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389520} {:answer/id #uuid "8137e0c5-1440-5348-a3f6-f96860233599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389521} {:answer/id #uuid "6eea4516-42fb-5185-853e-429392d0e13c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389522} {:answer/id #uuid "1720add8-c002-5c85-b431-35fa9200f452" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389523} {:answer/id #uuid "5ec4361d-c58f-5b04-80ef-1a4a55f43f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ec4361d-c58f-5b04-80ef-1a4a55f43f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389524} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ebc0e1f-5e97-5290-8156-5abbc7c3ef25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389519}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b9e45fcb-4a47-5dc3-ae3f-636d48328fa1" :question/math-academy-id "q-164441" :question/problem "$$\nf(x,z)=⟨x,\\,\\text{___},\\,z⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(x,z)$ above parametrizes the parabolic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $y=12{x}^{2}.$ What is the second component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "For any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,z) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨x,\\,12{x}^{2},\\,z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the second component of $f$ is $12{x}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389525 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73c57d5c-a186-5182-951a-b3f85487caeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389527} {:answer/id #uuid "1f864458-d395-5710-9718-008110d8e93b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389528} {:answer/id #uuid "0021c5a0-2342-5a2a-adac-8476ca592221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389529} {:answer/id #uuid "1602f014-a557-5551-9efb-7af44884ed34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389530} {:answer/id #uuid "a4cdf78f-30ac-56bf-91f8-1d994c3a2eae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f864458-d395-5710-9718-008110d8e93b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389528} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cb314a1-d9e4-51ef-9694-2ebcbc7cbfc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2fca6b56-70a9-5f2f-9046-3f8fb6cda9cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-164450" :question/problem "$$\nf(y,z)=⟨\\text{___},\\,y,\\,z⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(y,z)$ above parametrizes the parabolic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $8{z}^{2}=x.$ What is the first component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "For any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(y,z) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8{z}^{2},\\,y,\\,z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the first component of $f$ is $8{z}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389532 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "980f0e6e-b727-5884-9358-8f4cc871929f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389534} {:answer/id #uuid "0fd57ebb-6b0c-59bf-a69b-ea61588fa5c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389535} {:answer/id #uuid "0c5a90d4-f70c-5dbb-86f2-5da3595c4717" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389536} {:answer/id #uuid "fc4ce062-cc41-523a-b403-73151b819608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389537} {:answer/id #uuid "3fca4567-695f-5afb-931c-d416f8324d89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c5a90d4-f70c-5dbb-86f2-5da3595c4717" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389536} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb03e48f-e4f7-56b0-b0ed-a15eec593f0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389533}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "59a480e6-23f1-5a37-b498-2c012faa9753" :question/math-academy-id "q-164521" :question/problem "$$\nf(t,y)=⟨\\text{_____},\\,y,\\,2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(t,y)$ above parametrizes one sheet of the hyperbolic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as ${z}^{2}-{x}^{2}=4$ for $z\\ge 2.$ What is the first component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the hyperbola ${z}^{2}-{x}^{2}=4$ for $z\\ge 2$ in $xz$-plane has the parametrization\n\n$$\n⟨x,z⟩=⟨2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})\n$$\n\nsince \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =(2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t)^{2}-(2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)^{2} \\\\  & =4{sec}^{2}⁡t-4{tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =4({sec}^{2}⁡t-{tan}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t,y) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y,\\,2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the first component of $f$ is $2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389539 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "707fbf1b-bf7d-5995-b7cc-be64436a3be2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{sinh}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389541} {:answer/id #uuid "d22e14ca-11b5-5af0-a855-e0dc3f5271d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389542} {:answer/id #uuid "1adc692e-fe37-5019-893d-bd451359ba0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389543} {:answer/id #uuid "c552ac7b-ee72-589e-9065-cf0a29c3f734" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389544} {:answer/id #uuid "ec6ee24c-0ae3-5eec-973f-6e3492e4e1fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d22e14ca-11b5-5af0-a855-e0dc3f5271d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389542} :answer-field/id #uuid "bea9a704-6834-5c1c-808b-11ae8ac08e51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389540}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "aefa1f59-5dce-5a67-8312-bce584cb45c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-164522" :question/problem "$$\nf(t,z)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\text{_____},\\,z⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(t,z)$ above parametrizes the elliptic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $9{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=36.$ What is the second component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the ellipse \n\n$$\n9{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=36\\,⟹\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1\n$$\n\nin $xy$-plane has the parametrization\n\n$$\n⟨x,y⟩=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ),\n$$\n\nsince \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36} & =\\frac{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}}{36} \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t,z) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in [0,2\\pi )$ and $z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the second component of $f$ is $6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389553 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ed22918-85fb-5c79-9620-31cecfbbc27e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389555} {:answer/id #uuid "d4533c8f-a193-52ed-a9d9-fc9ccfbdbf2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389556} {:answer/id #uuid "974a57ae-291f-5842-95b3-64380db1d779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389557} {:answer/id #uuid "814a367c-72f0-5937-973d-1f16f3d1e3d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389558} {:answer/id #uuid "487b991c-c37d-5069-8337-bf2040028617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4533c8f-a193-52ed-a9d9-fc9ccfbdbf2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389556} :answer-field/id #uuid "20d86410-beeb-5cce-9a2f-324bd43cac89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "353926d7-638c-5e50-a022-4791f5ce8a3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-164524" :question/problem "$$\nf(t,z)=⟨5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\text{_____},\\,z⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(t,z)$ above parametrizes the elliptic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1.$ What is the second component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1$ in $xy$-plane has the parametrization\n\n$$\n⟨x,y⟩=⟨5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ),\n$$\n\nsince \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =\\frac{(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{25{cos}^{2}⁡t}{25}+\\frac{4{sin}^{2}⁡t}{4} \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t,z) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in [0,2\\pi )$ and $z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the second component of $f$ is $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551486 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d6336cf-f5dc-5c3c-8391-cf64d981595d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551484} {:answer/id #uuid "4deb3727-4b1a-53a0-8e6d-1915184259de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551489} {:answer/id #uuid "86073499-e653-5bf4-93a3-e32cbf4a2e8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551499} {:answer/id #uuid "c39ba631-2606-5594-bef2-80653d9a5d19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551511} {:answer/id #uuid "fb0dfc35-2b11-5072-992f-435169ab1d2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/val