1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t,x) & =⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨x,\\,8\\sec  t,\\,5\\tan  t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $$\n\\displaystyle t \\in \\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\n$$ and $x \\in (-\\infty, \\infty).$\n\nTherefore, the second component of $f$ is $8\\sec{t}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565646 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48521c14-8239-5605-8eee-dc106fdddfa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565639} {:answer/id #uuid "736a7003-73f5-54a6-baf3-179c2433ae44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7 t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565643} {:answer/id #uuid "8b7f33a7-d51e-5bf5-9e8b-0e744c3d15cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7 \\sec{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565645} {:answer/id #uuid "91ee3cc9-4495-554d-a1c1-91d099a2b2f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565647} {:answer/id #uuid "94be9b53-184b-56b5-ae6d-ba3581dd9046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7 \\csc{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565648}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b7f33a7-d51e-5bf5-9e8b-0e744c3d15cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7 \\sec{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565645} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1e8ce2b-fbce-5b19-aba7-80bf2063b065" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565657}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8eae8208-ee78-5906-94ee-3651010a62b2" :question/problem "$$\nf(t,y) = ⟨  \\text{_____} ,\\,  y,\\, 8\\tan{t}⟩, \\qquad t\\in\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(t,y)$ above parametrizes one sheet of the hyperbolic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $\\frac{x^2}{49} - \\frac{z^2}{64} = 1$ for $x \\ge 7.$ What is the first component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the hyperbola $\\frac{x^2}{49} - \\frac{z^2}{64} = 1$ for $x \\ge 7$ in $xz$-plane has the parametrization\n\n$$\n⟨ x ,\\, z ⟩ = ⟨  7\\sec{t} ,\\, 8\\tan{t}⟩,\n\n\\qquad t \\in \\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\n$$\n\nsince \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{49}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{64} & =\\frac{(7\\sec  t)^{2}}{49}-\\frac{(8\\tan  t)^{2}}{64} \\\\  & =\\frac{49\\sec^{2} t}{49}-\\frac{64\\tan^{2} t}{64} \\\\  & =\\sec^{2} t-\\tan^{2} t \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t,y) & =⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7\\sec  t,\\,y,\\,8\\tan  t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $$\n\\displaystyle t \\in \\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\n$$ and $y \\in (-\\infty, \\infty).$\n\nTherefore, the first component of $f$ is $7\\sec{t}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565652 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e9a9c63-d305-58f8-8939-de108bb574cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5} \\tan{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565637} {:answer/id #uuid "6f16e128-6266-5f70-8227-081372751497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5} \\csc{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565642} {:answer/id #uuid "9f93c92c-a391-5755-9a25-50ae2ca5eedc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565651} {:answer/id #uuid "ce48e565-2479-54eb-adad-0a5d2ff7d737" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 \\tan{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565658} {:answer/id #uuid "fe6069b8-3773-5c7a-b2aa-166a308da736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e9a9c63-d305-58f8-8939-de108bb574cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5} \\tan{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565637} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bd493ce-d4b7-506d-b012-7455d30301fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565636}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a2175c09-8ec0-5078-bc64-ae30286c4168" :question/problem "$$\nf(t,y)=⟨3\\sec  t,\\,y,\\,\\text{_____}⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(t,y)$ above parametrizes one sheet of the hyperbolic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $5{x}^{2}-9{z}^{2}=45$ for $x\\ge 3.$ What is the third component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the hyperbola\n\n$$\n5{x}^{2}-9{z}^{2}=45\\,⇒\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nfor $x\\ge 3$ in $xz$-plane has the parametrization\n\n$$\n⟨x,\\,z⟩=⟨3\\sec  t,\\,\\sqrt{5}\\tan  t⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})\n$$\n\nsince \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}} & =\\frac{(3\\sec  t)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(\\sqrt{5}\\tan  t)^{2}}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\sec^{2} t}{9}-\\frac{5\\tan^{2} t}{5} \\\\  & =\\sec^{2} t-\\tan^{2} t \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t,y) & =⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\sec  t,\\,y,\\,\\sqrt{5}\\tan  t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the third component of $f$ is $\\sqrt{5}\\tan  t.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565653 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b8e6533-7a71-5556-9b88-e7c0bfbbc1cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565633} {:answer/id #uuid "3f1142c2-732f-593d-beff-e9b73491dec1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\csc{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565638} {:answer/id #uuid "9c89faac-ddbb-5fe3-9dbd-4dd1c60aa8e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 t^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565650} {:answer/id #uuid "b44c5465-113f-5a68-ae84-3d7fb33eb9f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565654} {:answer/id #uuid "b8a2104b-163a-5c32-afd9-450b52dbdc88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\tan{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8a2104b-163a-5c32-afd9-450b52dbdc88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\tan{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565655} :answer-field/id #uuid "200010da-b078-592a-bdb2-ef576560b25d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565630}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a9f70865-2547-53bd-9c4a-85ac6829b744" :question/problem "$$\nf(t,z)=⟨\\text{_____},\\,2\\sec  t,\\,z⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(t,z)$ above parametrizes one sheet of the hyperbolic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as ${y}^{2}-{x}^{2}=4$ for $y\\ge 2.$ What is the first component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the hyperbola ${y}^{2}-{x}^{2}=4$ for $y\\ge 2$ in $xy$-plane has the parametrization\n\n$$\n⟨x,\\,y⟩=⟨2\\tan  t,\\,2\\sec  t⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})\n$$\n\nsince \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =(2\\sec  t)^{2}-(2\\tan  t)^{2} \\\\  & =4(\\sec^{2} t-\\tan^{2} t) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t,z) & =⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\tan  t,\\,2\\sec  t,\\,z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and $z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the first component of $f$ is $2\\tan  t.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565656 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20bf054f-3881-5709-ae5d-276405173f23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565631} {:answer/id #uuid "2346125c-ce7f-5f32-bb38-d8b81214344c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565632} {:answer/id #uuid "4e752bf2-a4ad-5dc2-8156-89b46f3d8939" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 \\csc{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565640} {:answer/id #uuid "538e832b-3549-55fc-9398-cba6a9b2086d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 \\sec{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565641} {:answer/id #uuid "f478fcd6-c813-5a35-8833-4087ee7127af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "538e832b-3