in{aligned}{z}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+\\frac{(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}}{25} \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t,x) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨x,\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in [0,2\\pi )$ and $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the third component of $f$ is $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186606807 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f16846f-5b70-5f3e-bfcd-98e57d75945a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606201} {:answer/id #uuid "608e01dc-bc24-5df5-aefb-3157145af0b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606342} {:answer/id #uuid "951728e6-3753-5941-813c-df8dd3d20609" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606458} {:answer/id #uuid "c68f09cb-bd0d-5b40-a7a2-fbc493107524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606552} {:answer/id #uuid "ca59893a-a14a-53e9-a6a6-13514da2b277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca59893a-a14a-53e9-a6a6-13514da2b277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606561} :answer-field/id #uuid "04a8e78b-cdbc-502e-98f5-b40abc13efb1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "22fbb0c0-b71c-56c8-9c26-43df6ce1581b" :question/math-academy-id "q-164451" :question/problem "$$\nf(x,y)=⟨x,\\,y,\\text{___}\\,⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(x,y)$ above parametrizes the parabolic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $5{y}^{2}=z.$ What is the third component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "For any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨x,\\,y,\\,5{y}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the third component of $f$ is $5{y}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186606810 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98a6dab8-eac0-5586-b56c-b080838910dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606467} {:answer/id #uuid "bddedb9b-8de9-5006-8fd9-7a5bc0efda01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606532} {:answer/id #uuid "c166cd3a-b85e-542f-9686-9d2e279e6872" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606539} {:answer/id #uuid "d91b1969-e75d-548c-b721-d1c569a93d0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606596} {:answer/id #uuid "fed796f3-1aab-5ff3-b564-922d825a5f95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fed796f3-1aab-5ff3-b564-922d825a5f95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606663} :answer-field/id #uuid "8296ef51-9a0d-536f-af90-7d10f69b8dd7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606741}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2546cccc-d039-5cb9-a144-ca3b62213170" :question/math-academy-id "q-164444" :question/problem "$$\nf(t,z)=⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\text{_____},\\,z⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(t,z)$ above parametrizes one sheet of the hyperbolic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}-{x}^{2}=1$ for $y\\ge 6.$ What is the second component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}-{x}^{2}=1$ for $y\\ge 6$ in $xy$-plane has the parametrization\n\n$$\n⟨x,y⟩=⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,6\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})\n$$\n\nsince \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}-{x}^{2} & =\\frac{(6\\operatorname{sec}⁡t)^{2}}{36}-(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{36{sec}^{2}⁡t}{36}-{tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡t-{tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t,z) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,6\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and $z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the second component of $f$ is $6\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186606814 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a3c0ccc-d0c2-52a5-a87d-406c7b403cfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606157} {:answer/id #uuid "3d6e193f-7023-5120-9ca5-160a99f2d6f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606269} {:answer/id #uuid "6869fe4d-f135-58b4-a97f-91b016beb10d" :answer/type {:db/id 