r/value "7z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606576}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d10420e8-6dcb-5e6b-ba33-d333dd599e94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606571} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b438a34-0288-5516-8f71-fb6891b6f58b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606713}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a5258f05-2242-527c-80be-bc39e4d71d51" :question/math-academy-id "q-164453" :question/problem "$$\nf(x,z)=⟨x,\\,\\text{___},\\,z⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(x,z)$ above parametrizes the parabolic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $7{z}^{2}=y.$ What is the second component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "For any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,z) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨x,\\,7{z}^{2},\\,z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the second component of $f$ is $7{z}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186606876 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36668f43-30a3-5486-bf9a-18e8c927d97e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606256} {:answer/id #uuid "4f59b908-3bf1-568e-9d31-0248470956da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606313} {:answer/id #uuid "7e556801-6d1b-501b-a215-e1ee7b2a28d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606409} {:answer/id #uuid "daf29590-237b-576b-8a46-95e2b0673683" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\operatorname{sinh}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606604} {:answer/id #uuid "ec55040b-1f10-5448-872b-cfa4f8fadf60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec55040b-1f10-5448-872b-cfa4f8fadf60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606631} :answer-field/id #uuid "3be6f516-4382-563f-86a1-6a91125f4120" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186606696}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a6212759-cbba-5bc3-9250-7f50b4a1f20e" :question/math-academy-id "q-164535" :question/problem "$$\nf(t,x)=⟨x,\\text{_____},\\,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(t,x)$ above parametrizes the elliptic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $16{y}^{2}+9{z}^{2}=144.$ What is the second component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the ellipse \n\n$$\n16{y}^{2}+9{z}^{2}=144\\,⟹\\,\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16}=1\n$$\n\nin $yz$-plane has the parametrization\n\n$$\n⟨y,z⟩=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ),\n$$\n\nsince \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16} & =\\frac{(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}}{16} \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t,x) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨x,\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in [0,2\\pi )$ and $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the second component of $f$ is $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642351 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3711e5f0-b871-53e9-b993-0526150f9a50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641920} {:answer/id #uuid "39ea66c0-e6bb-5e34-9ef4-ca5db2e5af4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641928} {:answer/id #uuid "5a4e1114-5b97-5903-913c-e87a805197ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641970} {:answer/id #uuid "99375689-1957-5b96-9b62-de0a0c53face" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642066} {:answer/id #uuid "ca99accf-df21-5c8b-8c00-31f62745305c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642126}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99375689-1957-5b96-9b62-de0a0c53face" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642066} :answer-field/id #uuid "080dd009-bc62-5375-85b9-9e40710642d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642204}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a5ac922e-1010-52fd-91b5-996400f5d210" :question/math-academy-id "q-164533" :question/problem "$$\nf(t,x)=⟨x,\\text{_____},\\,8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(t,x)$ above parametrizes the elliptic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{64}=1.$ What is the second component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the ellipse $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{64}=1$ in $yz$-plane has the parametrization\n\n$$\n⟨y,z⟩=⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ),\n$$\n\nsince \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{64} & =\\frac{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}}{64} \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t,x) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨x,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in [0,2\\pi )$ and $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the second component of $f$ is $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693421 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16addf70-baa8-5c61-a31e-f2e62d7c8a3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693406} {:answer/id #uuid "452d8e5b-9b39-51d8-8f5e-7c5e56a16c8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693411} {:answer/id #uuid "4ad9468a-115d-59ca-a85e-3c03a4810366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693412} {:answer/id #uuid "52abd163-3699-58cf-89a9-03f5a8c7a4c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693413} {:answer/id #uuid "6b3ed68a-9ab6-5f0c-bbb2-62ba235c553e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16addf70-baa8-5c61-a31e-f2e62d7c8a3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693406} :answer-field/id #uuid "755f8121-c882-5b00-b381-144945e143be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693418}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b58cbf32-c70b-525d-bd58-e9f534382ccb" :question/problem "The function\n\n$$\n\\mathbf f(t,z)=\\langle \\text{_____},\\,3\\tan t,\\,z\\rangle\n$$\n\nwith $-\\pi/2<t<\\pi/2$ and $z\\in\\mathbb R$ parametrizes the sheet of the hyperbolic cylinder\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{4}-\\frac{y^2}{9}=1,\\qquad x\\ge 2.\n$$\n\nUse $\\sec^2 t-\\tan^2 t=1$ and $\\sec t\\ge 1$ on this interval. What is the first component of $\\mathbf f$?" :question/worked-solution "The free coordinate $z$ controls movement parallel to the cylinder's axis. In the $xy$-plane, substituting $y=3\\tan t$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{4}=1+\\tan^2 t=\\sec^2 t.\n$$\n\nSince $x\\ge 2$ and $\\sec t\\ge 1$ on the given interval, choose the positive root: $x=2\\sec t$. Thus\n\n$$\n\\mathbf f(t,z)=\\langle 2\\sec t,\\,3\\tan t,\\,z\\rangle.\n$$\n\nSubstitution verifies the equation:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(2\\sec t)^2}{4}-\\frac{(3\\tan t)^2}{9}\n=\\sec^2 t-\\tan^2 t=1.\n$$\n\nAs $t$ runs through $(-\\pi/2,\\pi/2)$, $3\\tan t$ takes every real value and $2\\sec t$ gives the corresponding point on the positive branch. Letting $z$ range over all real numbers gives the whole sheet. The first component is $2\\sec t$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693424 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ca82780-07e0-50f7-8205-179c6c1bd472" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693408} {:answer/id #uuid "4272b8d2-a5a5-58b2-a11f-608ab03dadd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693410} {:answer/id #uuid "71fe7e42-e2cf-5da9-8c28-dead07e88a1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693417} {:answer/id #uuid "8643c465-1243-596f-b448-5caa03400e5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693419} {:answer/id #uuid "aba5d830-bc9f-5425-9873-12071631810e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4272b8d2-a5a5-58b2-a11f-608ab03dadd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693410} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bfdd5c9-055d-5794-b36e-f16658d09176" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693407}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d66c53fb-31c2-5fb5-b231-1ecbc974a98b" :question/problem "The function\n\n$$\n\\mathbf f(x,t)=\\langle x,\\,\\text{_____},\\,\\sqrt{2}\\tan t\\rangle\n$$\n\nwith $-\\pi/2<t<\\pi/2$ and $x\\in\\mathbb R$ parametrizes the sheet of the hyperbolic cylinder\n\n$$\n2y^2-3z^2=6,\\qquad y\\ge\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the second component of $\\mathbf f$?" :question/worked-solution "Divide the Cartesian equation by $6$ to identify the two squared scale factors:\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^2}{3}-\\frac{z^2}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nThe cross-section lies in the $yz$-plane and $x$ is free. With $z=\\sqrt{2}\\tan t$, the normalized equation gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^2}{3}=1+\\frac{(\\sqrt{2}\\tan t)^2}{2}\n=1+\\tan^2 t=\\sec^2 t.\n$$\n\nThe scale for $y$ is $\\sqrt{3}$, not $3$. Since $\\sec t\\ge 1$ on the given interval and $y\\ge\\sqrt{3}$, the correct sign is positive:\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{3}\\sec t.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\mathbf f(x,t)=\\langle x,\\,\\sqrt{3}\\sec t,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\tan t\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCheck directly in the original equation:\n\n$$\n2(\\sqrt{3}\\sec t)^2-3(\\sqrt{2}\\tan t)^2\n=6(\\sec^2 t-\\tan^2 t)=6.\n$$\n\nThe tangent coordinate takes every real $z$, the secant coordinate supplies the corresponding positive $y$, and arbitrary real $x$ extends this branch along the cylinder's axis. The second component is $\\sqrt{3}\\sec t$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693426 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "380bd172-2579-5d34-9b45-1e77dd61824e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693409} {:answer/id #uuid "6d1d94bc-cba5-508d-b706-8a9e038beb57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693415} {:answer/id #uuid "6dbb5884-76d9-5628-a769-88ca6d519e97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693416} {:answer/id #uuid "ba349c60-ef67-5198-a33b-bf5d0217c080" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693422} {:answer/id #uuid "c450b773-6a7b-5df7-9fd5-09caa38b8c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dbb5884-76d9-5628-a769-88ca6d519e97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693416} :answer-field/id #uuid "e096c4e2-703a-574f-8bb2-aedf210e1fad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693425}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f2fe2c2c-da80-5753-8bd1-8b11ec3e52b9" :question/problem "The function\n\n$$\n\\mathbf f(t,y)=\\langle \\text{_____},\\,y,\\,3\\sec t\\rangle\n$$\n\nwith $-\\pi/2<t<\\pi/2$ and $y\\in\\mathbb R$ parametrizes the sheet of the hyperbolic cylinder\n\n$$\n\\frac{z^2}{9}-\\frac{x^2}{4}=1,\\qquad z\\ge 3.\n$$\n\nWhat is the first component of $\\mathbf f$?" :question/worked-solution "The equation involves $x$ and $z$, so $y$ is the free coordinate. Substituting $z=3\\sec t$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{4}=\\frac{(3\\sec t)^2}{9}-1\n=\\sec^2 t-1=\\tan^2 t.\n$$\n\nThe choice $x=2\\tan t$ satisfies this relation for every $t$ in the given interval. Thus\n\n$$\n\\mathbf f(t,y)=\\langle 2\\tan t,\\,y,\\,3\\sec t\\rangle.\n$$\n\nChecking the base curve,\n\n$$\n\\frac{(3\\sec t)^2}{9}-\\frac{(2\\tan t)^2}{4}\n=\\sec^2 t-\\tan^2 t=1.\n$$\n\nSince $\\sec t\\ge 1$ on $(-\\pi/2,\\pi/2)$, the sheet condition $z\\ge 3$ holds. The tangent coordinate covers all real $x$, while arbitrary real $y$ extends the base curve along the cylinder's axis. The first component is $2\\tan t$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693601 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f976103-4e10-5cda-b355-ab349ea0a50d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693591} {:answer/id #uuid "248bb336-8b56-5f54-997e-50a47a6a36a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693592} {:answer/id #uuid "54b667f2-0537-5e3c-a1bf-ced228e9e56f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693594} {:answer/id #uuid "5d6d7242-ee5a-57b2-911f-b1e71d1ce202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693596} {:answer/id #uuid "7514f56e-05f9-5a46-a8d9-8ab800491cff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693598} {:answer/id #uuid "9250b3dc-3822-5218-b0ca-7e1c7e8a68b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d6d7242-ee5a-57b2-911f-b1e71d1ce202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693596} :answer-field/id #uuid "16860e66-7252-5f4c-80a5-7cda92809ba4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693590}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "96b6e345-b050-57c6-83a0-794c1f781e49" :question/problem "The function\n\n$$\nf(t,y)=\\langle \\text{_____},\\,y,\\,\\sqrt{3}\\sec t\\rangle\n$$\n\nwith $-\\pi/2<t<\\pi/2$ and $y\\in\\mathbb R$ parametrizes the sheet of the hyperbolic cylinder\n\n$$\n5z^2-3x^2=15,\\qquad z\\ge \\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the first component of $f$?" :question/worked-solution "Divide the Cartesian equation by $15$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{z^2}{3}-\\frac{x^2}{5}=1\n$$\n\nThe base curve uses $z$ and $x$; $y$ is the free coordinate. Substituting the supplied component gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{5}=\\frac{(\\sqrt{3}\\sec t)^2}{3}-1=\\sec^2 t-1=\\tan^2 t.\n$$\n\nChoose $x=\\sqrt{5}\\tan t$, which takes every real value on the given interval. This is the positive-tangent orientation used in the choices. The scale is $\\sqrt{5}=\\sqrt{5}$. Thus\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{5}\\tan t,\\qquad f(t,y)=\\langle \\sqrt{5}\\tan t,\\,y,\\,\\sqrt{3}\\sec t\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCheck in the normalized equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(\\sqrt{3}\\sec t)^2}{3}-\\frac{(\\sqrt{5}\\tan t)^2}{5}&=\\sec^2 t-\\tan^2 t\\\\&=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe secant coordinate satisfies the positive-sheet condition. The tangent coordinate ranges over all real values, and arbitrary real $y$ extends the base curve along the cylinder axis. Therefore the first component is $\\sqrt{5}\\tan t$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693602 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24c24dd8-8d4b-549a-bb4a-51247d2fd282" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693593} {:answer/id #uuid "55715973-2742-5351-8ae4-69f3e61fe9af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693595} {:answer/id #uuid "8677b7db-6f0b-50d0-af8c-fbaccef73eea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693599} {:answer/id #uuid "b7656293-96f4-5814-a18a-98503ce1ea28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693603} {:answer/id #uuid "d8fc2fd1-3cbc-5e2c-ad55-dd7a4d9cd54f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693604} {:answer/id #uuid "f930c818-cbb8-529d-b3e1-e0b034dea184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8fc2fd1-3cbc-5e2c-ad55-dd7a4d9cd54f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693604} :answer-field/id #uuid "71c785cd-a958-54b4-9710-5843d8780783" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693597}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "afc43eab-885c-5e9f-adfa-a2dd49ff1893" :question/problem "The function\n\n$$\nf(t,y)=\\langle \\text{_____},\\,y,\\,\\sqrt{7}\\tan t\\rangle\n$$\n\nwith $-\\pi/2<t<\\pi/2$ and $y\\in\\mathbb R$ parametrizes the sheet of the hyperbolic cylinder\n\n$$\n7x^2-3z^2=21,\\qquad x\\ge \\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the first component of $f$?" :question/worked-solution "Divide the Cartesian equation by $21$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{3}-\\frac{z^2}{7}=1\n$$\n\nThe base curve uses $x$ and $z$; $y$ is the free coordinate. Substituting the supplied component gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{3}=1+\\frac{(\\sqrt{7}\\tan t)^2}{7}=1+\\tan^2 t=\\sec^2 t.\n$$\n\nSince $x\\ge \\sqrt{3}$ and $\\sec t\\ge1$ on the given interval, take the positive root. The scale is $\\sqrt{3}=\\sqrt{3}$. Thus\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{3}\\sec t,\\qquad f(t,y)=\\langle \\sqrt{3}\\sec t,\\,y,\\,\\sqrt{7}\\tan t\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCheck in the normalized equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(\\sqrt{3}\\sec t)^2}{3}-\\frac{(\\sqrt{7}\\tan t)^2}{7}&=\\sec^2 t-\\tan^2 t\\\\&=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe secant coordinate satisfies the positive-sheet condition. The tangent coordinate ranges over all real values, and arbitrary real $y$ extends the base curve along the cylinder axis. Therefore the first component is $\\sqrt{3}\\sec t$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693612 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a156935-14db-5591-87e1-4d56128a189a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693617} {:answer/id #uuid "b8324c73-efe9-54c7-925e-a14a9933398f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693625} {:answer/id #uuid "b9de2383-fb6d-5b65-a23e-5ab5bd19fee8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693626} {:answer/id #uuid "d2a8956e-ad4e-5beb-baf1-d234aff21599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693629} {:answer/id #uuid "df96bc1a-a7bb-5458-826c-e37cb30da216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693631} {:answer/id #uuid "f95e6eb3-8783-5aa3-a5d0-7020ab587c4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df96bc1a-a7bb-5458-826c-e37cb30da216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693631} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d8eca51-18a6-5cff-9e50-3c8331ae6e3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693613}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4966d3cc-d2a3-58cd-bd19-aff11ae08e0d" :question/problem "The function\n\n$$\nf(t,x)=\\langle x,\\,\\text{_____},\\,2\\sec t\\rangle\n$$\n\nwith $-\\pi/2<t<\\pi/2$ and $x\\in\\mathbb R$ parametrizes the sheet of the hyperbolic cylinder\n\n$$\n\\frac{z^2}{4}-\\frac{y^2}{1}=1,\\qquad z\\ge 2.\n$$\n\nUse $\\sec^2 t-\\tan^2 t=1$. What is the second component of $f$?" :question/worked-solution "The equation is already normalized. The base curve uses $z$ and $y$; $x$ is the free coordinate. Substituting the supplied component gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^2}{1}=\\frac{(2\\sec t)^2}{4}-1=\\sec^2 t-1=\\tan^2 t.\n$$\n\nChoose $y=\\tan t$, which takes every real value on the given interval. This is the positive-tangent orientation used in the choices. The scale is $1=\\sqrt{1}$. Thus\n\n$$\ny=\\tan t,\\qquad f(t,x)=\\langle x,\\,\\tan t,\\,2\\sec t\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCheck in the normalized equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(2\\sec t)^2}{4}-\\frac{(\\tan t)^2}{1}&=\\sec^2 t-\\tan^2 t\\\\&=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe secant coordinate satisfies the positive-sheet condition. The tangent coordinate ranges over all real values, and arbitrary real $x$ extends the base curve along the cylinder axis. Therefore the second component is $\\tan t$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693621 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a47eabb-e050-5e6a-bb31-20e0f0f28457" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693610} {:answer/id #uuid "6a3217ef-0c1a-57c2-a324-000fa7a486c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693616} {:answer/id #uuid "8a865eda-46c6-5916-9722-af922f9998df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693622} {:answer/id #uuid "b4151c87-c2b5-55df-9ae9-7c7abce236c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693624} {:answer/id #uuid "cc3c1f71-f100-58b4-bc12-5c45432c6c5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693627} {:answer/id #uuid "e0c4e02a-b802-528f-bc6d-ba33f8b3ec90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a3217ef-0c1a-57c2-a324-000fa7a486c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693616} :answer-field/id #uuid "cceadbf2-0667-51ff-af85-33ed327da607" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693628}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8550c50a-8ab1-55ed-9e26-fca8fb68360b" :question/problem "The function\n\n$$\nf(t,y)=\\langle 3\\sec t,\\,y,\\,\\text{_____}\\rangle\n$$\n\nwith $-\\pi/2<t<\\pi/2$ and $y\\in\\mathbb R$ parametrizes the sheet of the hyperbolic cylinder\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{9}-\\frac{z^2}{16}=1,\\qquad x\\ge 3.\n$$\n\nUse $\\sec^2 t-\\tan^2 t=1$. What is the third component of $f$?" :question/worked-solution "The equation is already normalized. The base curve uses $x$ and $z$; $y$ is the free coordinate. Substituting the supplied component gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{z^2}{16}=\\frac{(3\\sec t)^2}{9}-1=\\sec^2 t-1=\\tan^2 t.\n$$\n\nChoose $z=4\\tan t$, which takes every real value on the given interval. This is the positive-tangent orientation used in the choices. The scale is $4=\\sqrt{16}$. Thus\n\n$$\nz=4\\tan t,\\qquad f(t,y)=\\langle 3\\sec t,\\,y,\\,4\\tan t\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCheck in the normalized equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(3\\sec t)^2}{9}-\\frac{(4\\tan t)^2}{16}&=\\sec^2 t-\\tan^2 t\\\\&=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe secant coordinate satisfies the positive-sheet condition. The tangent coordinate ranges over all real values, and arbitrary real $y$ extends the base curve along the cylinder axis. Therefore the third component is $4\\tan t$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693630 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "555e8b63-3660-575b-b616-5bc3c74329a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693614} {:answer/id #uuid "6082b31f-df65-5c56-b742-426ea82323d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693615} {:answer/id #uuid "7d690a46-2eba-52bb-b9b6-aac3d88689a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693618} {:answer/id #uuid "7f4c4b1f-d2c2-5d18-87de-c88dc493d37a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693620} {:answer/id #uuid "9e7fd304-f5d3-5e66-98dd-82befa82b0c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693623} {:answer/id #uuid "e440340d-884f-5185-b683-77413b856698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e440340d-884f-5185-b683-77413b856698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693634} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e882358-0e86-5c82-9a95-ca05ad2c0f7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693619}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d514ebb1-a67c-52a4-b2f7-e422f4576312" :question/problem "The function\n\n$$\nf(t,y)=\\langle \\tan t,\\,y,\\,\\text{_____}\\rangle\n$$\n\nwith $-\\pi/2<t<\\pi/2$ and $y\\in\\mathbb R$ parametrizes the sheet of the hyperbolic cylinder\n\n$$\n\\frac{z^2}{16}-\\frac{x^2}{1}=1,\\qquad z\\ge 4.\n$$\n\nUse $\\sec^2 t-\\tan^2 t=1$. What is the third component of $f$?" :question/worked-solution "The equation is already normalized. The base curve uses $z$ and $x$; $y$ is the free coordinate. Substituting the supplied component gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{z^2}{16}=1+\\frac{(\\tan t)^2}{1}=1+\\tan^2 t=\\sec^2 t.\n$$\n\nSince $z\\ge 4$ and $\\sec t\\ge1$ on the given interval, take the positive root. The scale is $4=\\sqrt{16}$. Thus\n\n$$\nz=4\\sec t,\\qquad f(t,y)=\\langle \\tan t,\\,y,\\,4\\sec t\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCheck in the normalized equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(4\\sec t)^2}{16}-\\frac{(\\tan t)^2}{1}&=\\sec^2 t-\\tan^2 t\\\\&=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe secant coordinate satisfies the positive-sheet condition. The tangent coordinate ranges over all real values, and arbitrary real $y$ extends the base curve along the cylinder axis. Therefore the third component is $4\\sec t$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693633 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1097e030-05cf-5eab-8eef-043df73a4ec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693607} {:answer/id #uuid "12d4dbb2-e7f9-5a8d-975d-3dafebca2a15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693608} {:answer/id #uuid "2c3fff2b-e1ee-57f3-918e-578d43c65969" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693611} {:answer/id #uuid "e8cee5e7-b985-5bc5-a49d-c32ef70de356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693635} {:answer/id #uuid "fbda4501-0e4c-5efb-8e70-3fdd0ebe2e3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693637} {:answer/id #uuid "ff66d7e7-8e10-58e7-8984-25f06617c589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1097e030-05cf-5eab-8eef-043df73a4ec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693607} :answer-field/id #uuid "26d2a154-edf3-52ce-bb83-318a66c66e1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693609}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e3ab36ea-348f-5ab5-a966-f76b064cacef" :question/problem "The function\n\n$$\nf(t,z)=\\langle 4\\tan t,\\,\\text{_____},\\,z\\rangle\n$$\n\nwith $-\\pi/2<t<\\pi/2$ and $z\\in\\mathbb R$ parametrizes the sheet of the hyperbolic cylinder\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^2}{1}-\\frac{x^2}{16}=1,\\qquad y\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nUse $\\sec^2 t-\\tan^2 t=1$. What is the second component of $f$?" :question/worked-solution "The equation is already normalized. The base curve uses $y$ and $x$; $z$ is the free coordinate. Substituting the supplied component gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^2}{1}=1+\\frac{(4\\tan t)^2}{16}=1+\\tan^2 t=\\sec^2 t.\n$$\n\nSince $y\\ge 1$ and $\\sec t\\ge1$ on the given interval, take the positive root. The scale is $1=\\sqrt{1}$. Thus\n\n$$\ny=\\sec t,\\qquad f(t,z)=\\langle 4\\tan t,\\,\\sec t,\\,z\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCheck in the normalized equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(\\sec t)^2}{1}-\\frac{(4\\tan t)^2}{16}&=\\sec^2 t-\\tan^2 t\\\\&=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe secant coordinate satisfies the positive-sheet condition. The tangent coordinate ranges over all real values, and arbitrary real $z$ extends the base curve along the cylinder axis. Therefore the second component is $\\sec t$."}]}
